<title>USA: UPS pilots union votes strike authorization.</title>
<headline>UPS pilots union votes strike authorization.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Independent Pilots Association said Tuesday that 94 percent of the nearly 2,000 pilots employed by United Parcel Service voted to authorise a strike if an agreement is not reached soon with the package delivery giant.</p>
<p>A strike count on Monday showed that all but 28 of the 1,874 pilots who cast ballots voted in favour of authorising a strike.</p>
<p>The pilots said the strike vote came a month after UPS &quot;suddenly&quot; withdrew its previous contract offer from the bargaining table and requested intervention by federal mediators.</p>
<p>UPS and the IPA have been negotiating since 1995. The pilots were scheduled to hold a conference call with reporters later on Tuesday.</p>
